5. Multi-Agent System
5.1 Agent design principles
Each agent must have:

One clear responsibility.

A defined input schema.

A defined output schema.

Approved tools.

Permission scope.

Maximum execution depth.

Token and cost limits.

Timeout limits.

Retry policy.

Human escalation conditions.

Versioned instructions.

Traceable actions.

Agents should not independently modify the same business state without coordination. A shared context layer is necessary so that one agent knows what another agent has already done.

