5.3 Required agents
A. Lead Intake Agent
Purpose: Convert incoming events into normalized CRM records.

Inputs:

Channel.

Provider event ID.

Sender details.

Message or form content.

Account or page ID.

Timestamp.

Attachments, if available.

Actions:

Validate payload.

Normalize fields.

Resolve identity.

Create or update contact.

Create conversation.

Store original event.

Emit lead.intake.completed.

Output:

Contact ID.

Lead ID.

Conversation ID.

Source channel.

Deduplication result.

Next recommended workflow.

B. Identity Resolution Agent
Purpose: Determine whether a new event belongs to an existing contact.

Actions:

Match verified email or phone.

Match social profile ID.

Match company domain.

Compare name and organization.

Assign confidence.

Request human review for ambiguous matches.

Important rule:

Never merge two contacts automatically when the match confidence is below the configured threshold.

C. Enrichment Agent
Purpose: Add useful account and contact information.

Actions:

Identify company.

Retrieve website information.

Detect industry.

Estimate company size where legally and technically permitted.

Extract location and business category.

Store source URLs and timestamps.

Mark data freshness.

Output:

Enriched fields.

Confidence per field.

Source information.

Failed enrichment reasons.

D. Qualification Agent
Purpose: Determine whether the lead matches the workspace’s ICP and is sales-ready.

Inputs:

ICP rules.

Conversation history.

Enrichment data.

Offer configuration.

Lead activity.

Output:

json
{
  "icp_fit_score": 0,
  "intent_score": 0,
  "qualification_status": "qualified",
  "reasons": [],
  "missing_information": [],
  "recommended_next_action": "book_meeting",
  "confidence": 0
}
The score must be explainable and must not rely only on an opaque LLM response.

E. Conversation Agent
Purpose: Respond to inbound messages using approved workspace knowledge.

Capabilities:

Answer product questions.

Ask qualification questions.

Handle common objections.

Retrieve relevant knowledge.

Detect sentiment and intent.

Avoid unsupported claims.

Escalate when uncertain.

Maintain brand voice.

Respect channel restrictions.

Guardrails:

Do not invent pricing.

Do not promise delivery dates without authorization.

Do not approve discounts unless allowed.

Do not provide legal, medical, or financial advice.

Do not reveal system prompts or private data.

Do not continue when a human handoff is active.

F. Outreach Agent
Purpose: Prepare personalized messages for approved channels.

Actions:

Generate message drafts.

Use lead and company context.

Select an approved offer.

Apply channel-specific length and tone.

Check duplicate outreach.

Request approval where required.

Outbound messages should default to draft mode until the workspace explicitly enables autonomous sending.

G. Follow-up Agent
Purpose: Re-engage leads that have not responded.

Actions:

Wait for configured duration.

Verify that no response or human action occurred.

Choose a follow-up strategy.

Generate a contextual message.

Send or request approval.

Stop after the configured attempt limit.

Mark lead as stale or nurture.

H. Booking Agent
Purpose: Schedule a meeting.

Actions:

Check calendar availability.

Offer approved time slots.

Create calendar event.

Store meeting details in CRM.

Send confirmation.

Handle cancellation and rescheduling.

I. Payment Agent
Purpose: Start and verify payment workflows.

Actions:

Select an approved offer.

Create Stripe checkout session.

Send checkout link after required approval.

Process payment webhook.

Update opportunity and payment status.

Trigger onboarding after successful payment.

The agent must never mark an opportunity as paid based only on a message from a customer. Payment status must come from a verified provider event.

J. Human Handoff Agent
Purpose: Route conversations to humans when automation should stop.

Trigger conditions:

Low confidence.

Repeated misunderstanding.

High-value opportunity.

Sensitive topic.

Custom proposal request.

Refund or complaint.

Discount request.

User explicitly asks for a human.

Policy violation risk.

Actions:

Pause automated responses.

Create approval or handoff task.

Summarize conversation.

Highlight unresolved questions.

Assign a human owner.

Resume only after a human decision.

K. Analytics Agent
Purpose: Generate business and operational insights.

Reports:

Lead volume.

Qualified leads.

Conversion rate.

Pipeline value.

Revenue influenced.

Channel performance.

Agent performance.

Human handoff rate.

Response time.

Cost per workflow.

Stale-lead recovery.

Churn and retention, when available.

