6.2 Lead intake workflow
text
Receive provider event
→ Verify signature
→ Check idempotency key
→ Normalize payload
→ Resolve contact identity
→ Create or update CRM records
→ Store message
→ Load workspace configuration
→ Run qualification
→ Route next action
→ Emit workflow result
Acceptance criteria:

Duplicate webhook events do not create duplicate leads.

Failed enrichment does not lose the original lead.

Every step is retryable.

The workflow can resume after deployment or server failure.

The complete execution is visible in the trace.

6.3 Conversation workflow
text
Message received
→ Load conversation state
→ Check human-handoff lock
→ Retrieve relevant knowledge
→ Classify intent
→ Generate response
→ Apply policy checks
→ Decide draft, send, or escalate
→ Save message and action
→ Update CRM
6.4 Stale conversation workflow
text
Conversation becomes inactive
→ Wait configured duration
→ Check for new messages
→ Check whether the opportunity changed
→ Generate follow-up
→ Apply sending policy
→ Send or request approval
→ Wait again
→ Mark nurture, cold, or escalate
6.5 Human approval workflow
text
Agent proposes action
→ Policy engine evaluates risk
→ Create approval request
→ Notify reviewer
→ Pause workflow
→ Reviewer approves, edits, rejects, or expires request
→ Resume or terminate workflow
→ Record decision in audit log
6.6 Booking workflow
text
Lead requests a meeting
→ Check qualification status
→ Retrieve calendar availability
→ Offer slots
→ Lead selects slot
→ Create calendar event
→ Update CRM
→ Send confirmation
→ Schedule reminder
6.7 Payment workflow
text
Lead accepts offer
→ Verify offer and price
→ Create checkout session
→ Request approval if required
→ Send payment link
→ Receive verified Stripe webhook
→ Update payment and opportunity
→ Trigger onboarding
