14. Non-Functional Requirements
14.1 Reliability
Webhook processing must be idempotent.

Failed steps must retry with backoff.

Workflows must resume after application restarts.

External side effects must use idempotency keys.

Failed workflows must be visible and replayable.

Provider outages must not destroy lead data.

14.2 Performance
Initial targets:

API p95 response time below 500 ms for non-AI operations.

Lead intake acknowledgment below 2 seconds.

Agent response target below 10 seconds for normal conversations.

Dashboard page load below 3 seconds.

Workflow status updates visible within 5 seconds.

Background enrichment may execute asynchronously.

14.3 Scalability
The system should support:

Multiple tenants.

Multiple agents per tenant.

Multiple concurrent workflows.

Queue-based background processing.

Per-tenant rate limits.

Per-tenant cost budgets.

Horizontal API scaling.

Separate worker scaling.

